'''Level 1313''' was a level on the [[Ecumenopolis|metropolitan]] [[Planet|world]] of [[Coruscant]], so named because it was located one thousand, three hundred, and thirteen levels from the core of Coruscant, which was accessed by the [[underworld portal]]. It was part of Coruscant's criminal [[Coruscant Underworld|underworld]] and was the location of numerous crimes.<ref name="Dark Disciple" /> 1313 was Coruscant's most infamous level, a dungeon so deep that the world above forgot about it, filled with shattered conduits, fungus on the walls, and criminal gangs.<ref name="aftermath">[[Aftermath (novel)|''Aftermath'']]</ref> [[Trace Martez|Trace]] and [[Rafa Martez]] lived on level 1313 until they became indebted to [[Pintu Son-El]]<ref name="Gone with a Trace /> and left the planet in the [[Silver Angel|former's ship]] with [[Ahsoka Tano]].<ref name="Deal No Deal">{{TCW|Deal No Deal}}</ref>

{{Loc-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Originally, Level 1313 was developed by [[George Lucas]] for the [[Star Wars: Underworld|unproduced ''Star Wars'' live-action television series]] along with the character [[Saw Gerrera]]. However, due to budget concerns, the series was put on hold and Level 1313 was introduced in ''[[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]]''.<ref name="Episode guide">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/to-catch-a-jedi-episode-guide|text="To Catch a Jedi" Episode Guide &#124; The Clone Wars}}</ref> It was also the setting of the canceled video game, ''[[Star Wars: 1313]]''.<ref name="kotaku">{{WebCite|url=https://kotaku.com/disney-shuts-down-lucasarts-468473749|text=Disney Shuts Down LucasArts, Cancels Star Wars 1313 And Star Wars: First Assault|author=Schreier, Jason|date=2013-04-03|archivedate=20200321154742}}</ref>

